WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.339 --> 00:00:04.300
Being a human can be confusing.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:10.180
It can be hard to understand who you are and
why you do the things you do.

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:16.670
Hard to feel good about yourself when you
live with all of your flaws and afflictions.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:22.600
Hard to feel important in a world with others
who have their own sets of problems, often

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.570
too preoccupied with their own to care about
yours.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:33.760
And more often than not, because of all this,
it can feel like you are all alone.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:39.010
When we feel like this, it can be very easy
to lose our belief in love.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.700
To feel as though we do not deserve it.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:48.739
We might find ourselves subconsciously sabotaging
or pushing love away every time we get close

00:00:48.739 --> 00:00:50.880
enough to touch it.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:56.280
Because not until we learn that we are all
inherently worthy of love, and are able to

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:03.329
love ourselves unconditionally, will we ever
be able to accept love from someone else.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:09.249
And not until we accept love from someone
else, will someone else ever be able to truly

00:01:09.249 --> 00:01:13.999
love us and make us feel a little less alone.

00:01:13.999 --> 00:01:20.840
Learning how to love yourself allows you to
understand what love really is and how it

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:21.840
works.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.770
Loving yourself does not mean that you think
you’re better than others.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.899
It does not mean that you are always happy.

00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:31.899
And it does not mean that you think you are
perfect.

00:01:31.899 --> 00:01:39.289
It means that you know your flaws and struggles,
but still value and appreciate who you are,

00:01:39.289 --> 00:01:45.340
what you have, and your efforts to do the
best you can and make the most of life, despite

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:46.979
it all.

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:52.179
When you understand this for yourself, you
understand that the same applies to loving

00:01:52.179 --> 00:01:53.959
someone else.

00:01:53.959 --> 00:01:59.520
You understand how to both give love and accept
love.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:05.560
The truth is, we don’t need any permission
or achievement to be worthy of love.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:12.269
We are all alive and regardless of where we
came from and what we have done or gone through,

00:02:12.269 --> 00:02:19.680
being alive is the only permission you need
to feel like you are worthy of being alive.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:25.819
The inability to love one’s own self and
embrace the unconditional premise of love

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:34.150
is one of the biggest reasons why people struggle
to find and sustain successful relationships.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:40.409
It is why a person might get irritated by
the subtlest of their partner’s quirks.

00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:44.989
Why couples might fight over silly, trivial
things.

00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:51.829
Why couples distance over time or leave out
important parts of who they are and what they

00:02:51.829 --> 00:02:53.400
want in life.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.500
Why one might betray the other and have an
affair.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:04.780
Or why when the initial lustfulness of a relationship
goes away, often the love dies with it.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:10.840
All because one or both individuals don’t
understand and believe that they are worthy

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:17.290
of love and therefore, they act out of the
insecurity and desperation that the void of

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:19.670
love creates.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:26.109
You simply cannot give someone something that
you do not have, and you cannot accept something

00:03:26.109 --> 00:03:29.959
that you do not believe in from someone else.

00:03:29.959 --> 00:03:36.480
If you do not have love for the self, you
do not have any love to give to someone else.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:42.930
And, if you do not believe you are worthy
of love, you will resist anyone’s attempt

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:44.790
to give you theirs.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:50.870
You will think that a person who claims to
love you must be deceitful or crazy.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:56.230
Or just hasn’t had enough of a chance to
see you for who you truly are.

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:58.239
But perhaps they have.

00:03:58.239 --> 00:04:34.590
Perhaps you are the one who hasn’t seen
yourself for who you truly are.

